The progress bars agents show in the chat, and their logs.

With this deployment's server (images/server/patches/0022-agent-progress.patch)
and runner (images/runner/patches/0014-agent-progress.patch), an agent can
call sys_session_progress with a label, a percentage when it can tell, and a
log file. The session snapshot's `progress` field and session.progress events
carry the session's bars into the chat store as agentProgress.

The newest bar shows above Working… while the agent works on the turn that
set it (lib/agentProgress.ts liveProgress), as one compact row: the label,
with a trailing count kept in view, the percentage, a thin line along the
bottom that fills to it or sweeps without one, and Log. A message from the
user starts a turn without one, already while it's on its way to the server:
otherwise the last turn's finished bar flashed above Working… right after
sending. Every other bar is finished, and AssistantBubble shows it as one
line at the end of the reply that ends its turn (placeFinishedProgress, by
time against the user's messages): ✓ or ✗, its last label and how long it
ran. Log opens the bar's lines, polled every 1.5 seconds from
GET /v1/sessions/{id}/progress/{bar}/log while open; they keep coming after
the turn, e.g. from a dev server. The tool's calls are titled
"Progress: <label>".

